<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
Matches the Octavi IFR-1 (ifr1.py: VID 0x04D8 / PID 0xE6D6, confirmed on
real hardware via `dumpsys usb` in the §3.1 spike, decimal 1240/59094 -
Android's <usb-device> resource takes decimal, not hex).

Referenced from AndroidManifest.xml's USB_DEVICE_ATTACHED intent-filter:
when a device matching this filter is plugged in, Android launches
MainActivity directly AND auto-grants USB permission for it - no runtime
permission dialog needed for the expected-hardware case. UsbHidInput still
calls UsbManager.requestPermission() itself as a fallback for the case
where the app is already running when the IFR-1 is attached (that path
does need the dialog, same as any other USB-host Android app).
-->
<resources>
    <usb-device vendor-id="1240" product-id="59094" />
</resources>
